{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 24, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem he succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. \n*Early Life* \nRaymond III was born around 1140 and was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem his mother was the daughter of Baldwin II King of Jerusalem and Armenian noblewoman Morphia. \n*Reign* \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli became the Count of Tripoli in 1152 after the death of his father he was around 12 years old at that time and his mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age. \n*Capture and Later Life* \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was captured by Nur ad-Din Zangi in 1164 during the Battle of Harim and was imprisoned for several years he was released in 1173 and resumed his rule as Count of Tripoli. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and was a strong supporter of the Haute Cour which was the high court of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. \n*Relationships and Alliances* \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli formed alliances with other Christian leaders in the region including the King of Jerusalem and the Prince of Antioch he also formed alliances with Muslim leaders including Nur ad-Din Zangi. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was a key figure in the Battle of Montgisard in 1177 where the Christian forces led by Baldwin IV King of Jerusalem defeated the Muslim forces led by Saladin. \n*Legacy* \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli died in 1187 and was succeeded by his nephew Raymond IV Count of Tripoli he is remembered as a strong and wise leader who played a significant role in the history of the County of Tripoli and the Kingdom of Jerusalem. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was also known for his military campaigns against the Muslim forces and his attempts to expand the territory of the County of Tripoli. \n*Military Campaigns* \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli led several military campaigns against the Muslim forces including the Battle of Harim in 1164 and the Battle of Montgisard in 1177. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was a skilled military leader and was able to defend the County of Tripoli against several Muslim attacks during his reign. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was also a patron of the arts and architecture and several buildings were constructed during his reign including the Castle of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -9.775113539944869e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0009117737063206732}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00015948931104503572}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.8347842693328857}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.48570793867111206}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.6589117646217346}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.00011693747364915907}, {"token": " H", "logprob": -0.0005989664932712913}, {"token": "odi", "logprob": -0.0027500689029693604}, {"token": "erna", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Jerusalem", "logprob": -0.0013872295385226607}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -0.020747656002640724}, {"token": " succeeded", "logprob": -0.5849766731262207}, {"token": " his", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " father", "logprob": -1.0013530300057027e-05}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.03810487315058708}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0620243102312088}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -7.